+| `harness-ts/test/models.test.ts` | `models::tests::*`, `models::tests::providers::*` (the provider-config cases need the `bedrock`, `anthropic` and `openai` features) | 105/111 | Google, Ollama and LiteLLM are not Rust v0.1 providers (#60): `maps google auto to the high thinking level`, `uses the google model id directly`, `adds the google googleSearch built-in tool for web_search`, `omits google built-in tools when web_search is off`, `does not warn when caching is supported for litellm`, `builds litellm with explicit caching and sets no cacheConfig`. For the same reason the Google, Ollama and LiteLLM rows are left out of `resolves the per-model levels for %s with effort %s`, `rejects a level the provider does not support`, `is high on %s` and `sends no reasoning field to %s, where high would be rejected`, and the Google row of `is true for openai, google and bedrock-mantle` asserts `false`. `rejects an effort outside the enum by name` is ported against `parse_effort` (P-833) |
+| `harness-ts/test/openai-cache.test.ts` | | 0/2 | both cases (`it.each` over the OpenAI and Mantle cache layouts) drive `createHarness` end to end; they belong with `create_harness` |
